-- title:
--   Logarithmic differentials inject the p-torsion of Pic⁰
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, for a prime $p$, and let $F$ be a field extension of $K$. Let $t \in F$ be transcendental over $K$, assume $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $K(t)$ generated by $t$, assume $F$ is separable over $K(t)$, and assume that the universal derivation sends $t$ to a nonzero element of $\Omega_{F/K}$. Here a place of $F/K$ is a valuation subring of $F$ which contains the image of $K$, is not all of $F$, and is a principal ideal ring; $\mathrm{ord}_v f$ is minus the logarithm of the value of $f$ under the associated $\mathbb{Z}^{m0}$-valued adic valuation; divisors are the finitely supported $\mathbb{Z}$-valued functions on places; and $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ is the group of degree-zero divisors modulo the principal ones, whose $p$-torsion subgroup is the set of classes killed by $p$. The assertion is that there exists an additive homomorphism $\varphi$ from this $p$-torsion subgroup to $\Omega_{F/K}$ which is injective and is such that each value $\varphi(c)$ has the form $f^{-1}\,df$ for some $f \in F$, $f \neq 0$, with $p \mid \mathrm{ord}_v f$ for every place $v$. Only the existence of such a $\varphi$ is asserted: the statement does not record how $f$ is related to a divisor representing $c$.
--
--   This is the classical embedding of the $p$-torsion of the Jacobian of a curve in characteristic $p$ into the space of differentials by means of logarithmic derivatives, in the function-field formulation. It is used to bound the $p$-torsion of $\mathrm{Pic}^0$, via [`AlgebraicCurve.Pic0.finite_torsion_char`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.Pic0.finite_torsion_char).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Pic0_exists_injective_addMonoidHom_torsion_dlog.lean

